I just kicked the edge of the table.

11
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:56,240
Help!

12
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Help!

13
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:05,280
Get away from me!

14
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:06,600
Help!

15
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:07,840
Police,

16
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:09,160
Police, help me!

17
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:11,160
Help, brother! Help!

18
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:12,960
Help!

19
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:15,440
Hey.

20
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:36,880
WITH DEEPEST CONDOLENCES, FROM POLICE
LIEUTENANT GENERAL ARTHIT PHAYOMYONG

21
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:12,360
-Hello, sir.
-Hello.

22
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:14,280
Thank you for honoring us by coming.

23
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:16,280
Don't think too much of it.

24
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:18,360
We're on the same side.

25
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:20,360
Please, come this way.

26
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:33,160
Thank you, nephew.

27
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:36,400
Actually…

28
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:38,160
I didn't want to bring this up right now,

29
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:40,040
but

30
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:41,720
we're running out of time.

31
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:44,040
The party sent me

32
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:46,200
to approach you

33
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:50,240
they'd like you to run for Provincial
Administrative Organization chairman,

34
00:05:50,840 --> 00:05:52,360
replacing the one who just retired.

35
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:55,040
What do you think?

36
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:57,600
Just managing the farm alone
already leaves me with no time.

37
00:05:58,160 --> 00:06:00,280
Perhaps it's better to find someone else?

38
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:02,680
But your nephew is helping manage things,
isn't he?

39
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:09,440
I'd hate to see your abilities
go to waste.

40
00:06:10,520 --> 00:06:11,720
But if you join us,

41
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:13,120
everyone

42
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:15,520
eats well together.

43
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:18,800
If someone else comes in instead…

44
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:22,720
who knows where the budget ends up.

45
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:25,360
You understand.

46
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:28,280
I see.

47
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:31,320
Let me get through
the funeral arrangements first,

48
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:33,120
then we can talk.

49
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:35,000
Alright.

50
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:36,680
I'll excuse myself.

51
00:06:36,760 --> 00:06:37,760
Of course.

52
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:49,600
Inspector.

53
00:06:51,520 --> 00:06:52,560
My condolences, Chawin.

54
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:08,560
-Hello, sir.
-Hello.

55
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:09,840
Well, Inspector,

56
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:11,680
two of our people are dead now.

57
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:13,440
Look at this,

58
00:07:14,560 --> 00:07:16,240
Mr. Chawin's only son.

59
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:19,600
And the Minister is already pressing me
for answers.

60
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:21,560
What am I supposed to tell him?

61
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:24,200
The team is working
as fast as they can, sir.

62
00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:29,840
Or do I need to wait
for more of our people to die first?

63
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:31,960
I'll find the perpetrator
as quickly as possible, sir.

64
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:33,120
Alright.

65
00:07:35,120 --> 00:07:36,240
See that you do.

66
00:07:36,320 --> 00:07:37,320
Yes, sir.

67
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:54,920
If there's anything I can do,
just say the word, Mr. Chawin.

68
00:07:58,240 --> 00:08:00,560
My condolences.

69
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:02,600
Thank you, teacher.

70
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:04,960
Que, take the teacher inside to sit down.

71
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,520
-Thank you.
-My condolences.

72
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:45,880
Thank you.

73
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:47,800
Thank you.

74
00:08:48,640 --> 00:08:50,200
Thank you.

75
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:54,200
Thank you.

76
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:58,240
I'll head off first, Chawin.

77
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:00,600
-Thank you.
-My condolences.

78
00:09:04,400 --> 00:09:05,600
Thank you.

79
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:13,360
Thank you, thank you.

80
00:09:16,920 --> 00:09:18,080
I'll be heading back too.

81
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:24,160
Pin.

82
00:09:24,840 --> 00:09:25,920
I'm going ahead.

83
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:30,960
Stay and help out here for a bit, okay?

84
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:36,880
Thank you.

85
00:09:45,280 --> 00:09:46,520
Pin,

86
00:09:47,560 --> 00:09:48,560
do you remember me?

87
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:54,560
We met at the café, right?

88
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,000
You remember.

89
00:09:58,240 --> 00:09:59,240
You see…

90
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:02,960
I actually wanted to talk to you
about your sister.

91
00:10:05,640 --> 00:10:09,560
Oh. I might not be ready
to talk about that yet.

92
00:10:10,160 --> 00:10:11,560
Maybe another time.

93
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:14,960
I have a feeling that

94
00:10:16,520 --> 00:10:18,760
Chee's case and Pan's disappearance
are connected somehow.

95
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:23,840
It might sound strange
coming from a police officer

96
00:10:25,320 --> 00:10:27,400
but sometimes instinct and

97
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:29,840
gut feeling have cracked many cases.

98
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:32,640
But right now,

99
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:35,480
I can't investigate anything
about Chee at all.

100
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:40,120
Please tell me what you need directly.

101
00:10:41,200 --> 00:10:42,200
You see…

102
00:10:43,480 --> 00:10:46,400
I need everything you know
about Pan and Chee.

103
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:51,640
As Pan's sister, you must know something.

104
00:10:51,960 --> 00:10:52,960
That information

105
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:56,080
could help me crack Chee's case,

106
00:10:57,440 --> 00:10:59,000
and if I crack Chee's case,

107
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:01,440
I'll find out

108
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,360
where your sister went.

109
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:08,320
How about this?

110
00:11:08,920 --> 00:11:10,120
Please give me your phone.

111
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:11,960
Save my number.

112
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:14,080
If anything comes up, call me.

113
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:11,160
Proud.

114
00:12:15,520 --> 00:12:16,920
Aren't you lonely?

115
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:20,720
Don't do something like this.

116
00:12:23,240 --> 00:12:24,520
The rumor about you
not being a straight man,

117
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:26,880
is it true?

118
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:04,120
Do you like it? Huh?

119
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:35,720
In the past week,

120
00:13:35,800 --> 00:13:39,360
another murder has occurred
in Waripasop district.

121
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:41,400
The latest victim is Mr. Joe.

122
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:44,080
Police officers are now urgently
searching for the perpetrator.

123
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:45,720
-News about the district?
-It is speculated

124
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:48,840
It's absolutely brutal.

125
00:13:49,080 --> 00:13:51,680
The ones dying are your friends, man.
Did you even know about this?

126
00:13:51,760 --> 00:13:52,960
where the head of a teenage gang

127
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:54,320
got brutally murdered a week before.

128
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:56,920
Look at that.
That killer is absolutely brutal.

129
00:13:57,960 --> 00:14:01,720
based on testimony from Mr. M
a survivor of the most recent incident,

130
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:06,600
the killer was wearing a raincoat
and had their face fully concealed,

131
00:14:06,680 --> 00:14:09,560
The likely pattern of the case
points toward a revenge killing

132
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:10,640
targeting the gang of teenagers,

133
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:12,800
a son of locally influential figure.

134
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:15,680
The police are urgently
searching for the culprit.

135
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:17,800
The public is asked not to panic.

136
00:14:18,040 --> 00:14:19,200
Anyone with information,

137
00:14:19,280 --> 00:14:20,800
please contact the police officers.

138
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:25,040
WARIPASOP, POLICE STATION

139
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:31,760
PAN

140
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:45,640
How far along is the Chee case, Som?

141
00:14:46,120 --> 00:14:47,120
Inspector.

142
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:50,960
Do you know
how much scrutiny I'm under

143
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:53,400
because of how slowly you're working?

144
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:57,280
What is this?

145
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:03,160
I gave you freedom to investigate,

146
00:15:03,560 --> 00:15:05,520
and you're spending your time
digging up old cases?

147
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:07,680
I believe

148
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:11,080
the disappearance of this girl
is connected

149
00:15:11,600 --> 00:15:13,200
to the deaths of Chee and his friends.

150
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:14,360
I don't care about old cases.

151
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:17,280
I need you to handle these two new ones.

152
00:15:17,360 --> 00:15:19,160
Have you been watching too many movies?

153
00:15:19,520 --> 00:15:20,800
You think this is some

154
00:15:20,880 --> 00:15:22,320
woman-comes-back-for-revenge story?

155
00:15:22,640 --> 00:15:23,680
Close this case.

156
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:26,360
You're the hotshot from Bangkok,
aren't you?

157
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:28,800
Don't think I'll go easy on you just
because you're a woman.

158
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:44,040
PAN

159
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:54,840
Pin.

160
00:15:54,920 --> 00:15:57,360
Have you seen Pan's photo?

161
00:15:57,640 --> 00:15:59,400
I wiped it down and now I can't find it.

162
00:16:00,560 --> 00:16:01,560
Huh?

163
00:16:04,160 --> 00:16:05,160
Mom.

164
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:07,040
It's been three years.

165
00:16:07,600 --> 00:16:09,520
Aren't you tired? I can't take it anymore.

166
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:13,120
Nothing is more exhausting than
having you as a daughter.

167
00:16:15,280 --> 00:16:16,720
Then why not just kill me
and be done with it.

168
00:16:17,840 --> 00:16:18,840
Hey.

169
00:16:19,840 --> 00:16:21,600
Don't you dare talk to me like that.

170
00:16:21,680 --> 00:16:22,840
And isn't it true?

171
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:25,600
You cursed child.

172
00:16:29,640 --> 00:16:30,640
Go on, keep insulting me.

173
00:16:32,120 --> 00:16:33,360
Your father died the moment you were born.

174
00:16:35,440 --> 00:16:37,320
He wanted to come see you being delivered,

175
00:16:37,400 --> 00:16:38,600
thought he was getting a son.

176
00:16:38,680 --> 00:16:39,680
And what did he get?

177
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:43,360
Happy?

178
00:16:44,760 --> 00:16:46,880
Your father died because of you, Pin.

179
00:16:48,280 --> 00:16:50,880
My husband died because of you!

180
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:55,520
Ever since you were born,

181
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:58,960
everyone I love has died!

182
00:16:59,840 --> 00:17:00,920
You jinx!

183
00:17:05,200 --> 00:17:06,600
Then should I just die too?

184
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:08,600
If I die,

185
00:17:09,280 --> 00:17:10,880
maybe Dad and Pan will come back.

186
00:17:14,720 --> 00:17:15,840
Can you actually do it?

187
00:17:16,320 --> 00:17:17,320
Huh?

188
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:20,160
What do you mean by that, Mom?

189
00:17:21,840 --> 00:17:24,400
Ugh! What are you going to do now?

190
00:17:25,200 --> 00:17:26,480
Isn't this enough?

191
00:17:27,320 --> 00:17:28,720
If you're not going to look for it,

192
00:17:29,240 --> 00:17:30,480
I'll look myself.

193
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:39,760
I threw it away myself!

194
00:17:40,800 --> 00:17:42,600
If I kept it, you'd keep being like this!

195
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:45,320
I can't do this anymore, Mom!

196
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:54,640
You threw it where?

197
00:18:54,720 --> 00:18:55,720
Mom.

198
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,400
Pan is dead.

199
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:10,360
Pan is dead, Mom.

200
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:11,560
No!

201
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:17,040
But I'm still here with you.

202
00:19:20,520 --> 00:19:21,800
Can you hear me?

203
00:19:22,720 --> 00:19:23,920
I'm still here with you.

204
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:25,120
Hey!

205
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:27,640
What is all this?

206
00:19:28,640 --> 00:19:31,560
Pan is dead! But I'm still here with you!

207
00:19:32,080 --> 00:19:33,200
Why do you only love Pan?

208
00:19:33,280 --> 00:19:35,240
Why have you never once cared about me?

209
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,560
So you want Pan to be dead, is that it?

210
00:19:40,040 --> 00:19:41,240
Huh?

211
00:20:18,600 --> 00:20:19,600
Hello.

212
00:20:20,040 --> 00:20:21,360
My condolences.

213
00:20:21,760 --> 00:20:22,760
Mr. Chawin.

214
00:20:22,960 --> 00:20:24,080
You too.

215
00:20:24,160 --> 00:20:25,840
I think we'll get to work together.

216
00:20:25,920 --> 00:20:28,000
-Yes, sir.
-Thank you.

217
00:20:29,760 --> 00:20:30,920
Thank you.

218
00:20:33,320 --> 00:20:34,640
Hello, everyone.

219
00:20:34,720 --> 00:20:37,440
Thank you very much for honoring us
with your presence at the funeral.

220
00:20:37,520 --> 00:20:38,880
Thank you.

221
00:20:38,960 --> 00:20:40,360
Please call me if you need anything.

222
00:20:40,880 --> 00:20:43,520
Please don't worry. If there's anything,

223
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:45,280
just let me know.

224
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:47,560
Yes, thank you.

225
00:20:49,240 --> 00:20:50,240
Hello.

226
00:21:09,840 --> 00:21:11,160
What are you doing here alone?

227
00:21:12,240 --> 00:21:13,240
Hey.

228
00:21:14,120 --> 00:21:15,120
How did you find me?

229
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:16,480
Are you a stalker?

230
00:21:17,840 --> 00:21:18,920
You love it.

231
00:21:19,560 --> 00:21:20,600
That's crazy.

232
00:21:21,680 --> 00:21:23,680
People are getting murdered
left and right these days.

233
00:21:25,320 --> 00:21:26,560
Aren't you scared?

234
00:21:29,280 --> 00:21:30,280
MR. SEKSAN PANNGERN

235
00:21:30,360 --> 00:21:31,720
This old man died
under the temple pavilion.

236
00:21:32,640 --> 00:21:35,000
No family, no home.

237
00:21:35,080 --> 00:21:36,080
The ones organizing his funeral

238
00:21:36,160 --> 00:21:38,200
are a group of trans women
from a Facebook page.

239
00:21:39,880 --> 00:21:41,000
They don't even know each other.

240
00:21:41,560 --> 00:21:42,600
How do you know all that?

241
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:46,160
The undertaker told me.

242
00:21:46,640 --> 00:21:47,760
He likes to buy pork.

243
00:21:52,920 --> 00:21:54,360
But you know what's funny?

244
00:21:55,840 --> 00:21:57,160
When he was alive,

245
00:21:58,000 --> 00:21:59,280
he despised trans people.

246
00:22:00,240 --> 00:22:01,440
But once he died…

247
00:22:02,560 --> 00:22:04,520
those differences
didn't mean anything anymore.

248
00:22:27,120 --> 00:22:28,280
Do you miss your dad?

249
00:22:31,360 --> 00:22:34,920
MR. CHAIYAPOP TREEWANICH

250
00:22:38,520 --> 00:22:39,520
Mmm.

251
00:22:44,720 --> 00:22:45,800
You know,

252
00:22:47,840 --> 00:22:48,840
my dad…

253
00:22:52,120 --> 00:22:55,040
my dad's car flipped
on the way to the hospital.

254
00:22:56,600 --> 00:22:58,000
The day Mom was giving birth to me.

255
00:22:58,640 --> 00:22:59,680
That's why

256
00:23:00,280 --> 00:23:01,600
Mom hates me so much.

257
00:23:05,280 --> 00:23:06,680
Blaming someone

258
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:10,400
is sometimes just a way
of running from grief.

259
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:12,720
But shouldn't

260
00:23:14,040 --> 00:23:15,840
all mothers love all their children?

261
00:23:18,320 --> 00:23:19,400
If you think about it…

262
00:23:21,320 --> 00:23:23,360
it's not that strange for a mother
to resent her daughter.

263
00:23:25,640 --> 00:23:28,640
Having to look at the person
who took away her youth

264
00:23:29,360 --> 00:23:31,120
while that person gets to live freely,

265
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:34,080
have the kind of young love

266
00:23:36,600 --> 00:23:38,160
she can never have again.

267
00:23:39,760 --> 00:23:41,000
What about Pan?

268
00:23:41,840 --> 00:23:43,040
Then why does she love Pan?

269
00:23:44,440 --> 00:23:46,000
Is it because Pan was beautiful?

270
00:23:46,400 --> 00:23:47,440
Educated?

271
00:23:47,880 --> 00:23:49,200
Looked like she had a bright future?

272
00:23:50,120 --> 00:23:51,760
So Mom wanted to live through Pan.

273
00:23:52,160 --> 00:23:53,240
Rather than just being a housewife

274
00:23:53,320 --> 00:23:54,560
stuck in a tiny district like this.

275
00:24:15,960 --> 00:24:17,280
Jeans,

276
00:24:17,360 --> 00:24:18,640
the other night…

277
00:24:31,360 --> 00:24:32,920
Don't say anything yet.

278
00:24:37,320 --> 00:24:38,520
How did you know?

279
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:43,600
There's nothing I wouldn't tell you, Pin.

280
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:47,440
Just not right now.

281
00:25:50,160 --> 00:25:51,600
I'll help you.

282
00:26:01,320 --> 00:26:02,400
That's it.

283
00:26:12,040 --> 00:26:13,320
You're doing well.

284
00:26:16,160 --> 00:26:17,200
Just like that.

285
00:26:26,480 --> 00:26:27,520
That's right.

286
00:26:33,760 --> 00:26:34,800
Good girl.

287
00:27:06,280 --> 00:27:07,640
The news is starting to play us.

288
00:27:08,920 --> 00:27:10,240
All those damn social media lunatics

289
00:27:11,320 --> 00:27:12,760
talking about our community.

290
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:15,120
Soon there'll be kids coming
to make content here.

291
00:27:16,440 --> 00:27:18,400
This isn't just
about the district's reputation.

292
00:27:20,040 --> 00:27:21,760
It affects my career,

293
00:27:22,240 --> 00:27:23,320
and yours too.

294
00:27:24,240 --> 00:27:25,480
I'll close the case as quickly as I can.

295
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:28,280
The perpetrator has prepared carefully.

296
00:27:28,360 --> 00:27:29,360
However careful they are,

297
00:27:30,840 --> 00:27:32,240
if you can't find them, just build one.

298
00:27:33,960 --> 00:27:35,000
What do you mean by that?

299
00:27:38,360 --> 00:27:39,680
Here in Waripasop

300
00:27:40,800 --> 00:27:42,240
we have our own way of handling things.

301
00:27:43,920 --> 00:27:45,120
Here in Waripasop

302
00:27:55,680 --> 00:27:56,880
CASE FILE

303
00:27:56,960 --> 00:27:59,400
STILL MISSING

304
00:28:05,680 --> 00:28:08,040
THE BODY SHOWED SIGNS OF A PAINFUL DEATH,
FINGERS WERE MISSING.

305
00:28:16,960 --> 00:28:19,840
IT WAS DISCOVERED
THAT THE GENITALS WERE MISSING.

306
00:28:29,520 --> 00:28:31,480
POLICE LIEUTENANT COLONEL
ARTHIT PAYOMYONG

307
00:28:47,720 --> 00:28:49,440
Oh, you're home.

308
00:28:49,520 --> 00:28:51,240
Come, come, eat quickly,

309
00:28:51,320 --> 00:28:53,320
Mom made all your favourites.

310
00:28:59,520 --> 00:29:01,520
Mom, are you okay? Did something happen?

311
00:29:01,600 --> 00:29:04,120
Of course I'm okay.
What a strange question.

312
00:29:04,520 --> 00:29:06,080
Here, quickly eat.

313
00:29:06,720 --> 00:29:08,000
Eat while it's hot.

314
00:29:16,280 --> 00:29:17,280
Mr. Chawin

315
00:29:17,800 --> 00:29:19,520
Mr. Chawin is such a good man, isn't he.

316
00:29:20,840 --> 00:29:22,720
Seeing him made me think of Chee.

317
00:29:25,440 --> 00:29:27,680
I understand the heart of a parent
who's lost a child.

318
00:29:28,960 --> 00:29:29,960
And Mr. Chawin

319
00:29:30,240 --> 00:29:33,640
he's handling it all so bravely.

320
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:35,320
Really remarkable.

321
00:29:35,400 --> 00:29:36,440
Mom, what are you on about.

322
00:29:38,880 --> 00:29:40,080
Hey.

323
00:29:42,640 --> 00:29:44,480
If I were to look after
Mr. Chawin as well,

324
00:29:45,120 --> 00:29:46,120
what would you think?

325
00:29:46,920 --> 00:29:47,920
Hmm?

326
00:29:48,560 --> 00:29:49,840
I lost a daughter,

327
00:29:50,600 --> 00:29:52,080
he lost a son.

328
00:29:53,520 --> 00:29:54,640
Looking after each other…

329
00:29:54,840 --> 00:29:55,840
that seems nice, doesn't it?

330
00:29:57,800 --> 00:29:58,800
Well?

331
00:30:03,720 --> 00:30:06,600
Here. Egg clear soup, your favourite.

332
00:30:09,160 --> 00:30:10,360
What now.

333
00:30:13,960 --> 00:30:16,000
Fine, I'll eat it myself.

334
00:30:37,680 --> 00:30:40,960
Are they coming?
Told ya to add since yesterday.

335
00:30:42,480 --> 00:30:43,520
Non.

336
00:30:44,120 --> 00:30:46,400
What. There's a party tonight.
Eight o'clock.

337
00:30:46,480 --> 00:30:47,800
-Okay, sure.
-See you later.

338
00:30:59,480 --> 00:31:00,560
Fah.

339
00:31:00,640 --> 00:31:01,880
Yeah?

340
00:31:01,960 --> 00:31:03,160
Party tonight.

341
00:31:03,240 --> 00:31:04,280
You better come.

342
00:31:05,640 --> 00:31:07,280
Why are you inviting people now?

343
00:31:07,880 --> 00:31:08,880
Nai,

344
00:31:08,960 --> 00:31:10,600
it's scary as hell out there.

345
00:31:10,920 --> 00:31:12,280
Two of our friends are already dead.

346
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:15,200
There'll be loads of people there.
What's there to be scared of?

347
00:31:16,480 --> 00:31:17,960
Yeah, yeah. Fine, I'll go.

348
00:31:18,920 --> 00:31:20,000
Be there at eight.

349
00:31:20,320 --> 00:31:21,560
Plenty of stuff.

350
00:31:21,640 --> 00:31:23,280
-See you.
-See you then.

351
00:31:24,800 --> 00:31:25,800
Wait.

352
00:31:28,720 --> 00:31:29,800
You're Nai, right?

353
00:31:33,400 --> 00:31:34,680
Why did you go to prison?

354
00:31:36,920 --> 00:31:37,960
You know what, officer,

355
00:31:38,560 --> 00:31:39,880
if I'd known you were a cop that day,

356
00:31:40,480 --> 00:31:41,720
I wouldn't have just changed your tire.

357
00:31:42,280 --> 00:31:43,560
I would've cut your brake line.

358
00:31:44,640 --> 00:31:46,720
I don't care why you hate cops.

359
00:31:47,320 --> 00:31:48,840
I want to know why you went to prison.

360
00:31:50,760 --> 00:31:52,920
It was a long time ago.
Why do you even want to know?

361
00:31:53,440 --> 00:31:55,160
The file says you shot someone
and nearly killed them.

362
00:31:55,240 --> 00:31:57,080
But the evidence doesn't add up.

363
00:31:57,520 --> 00:31:58,720
What really happened?

364
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:01,080
You don't need to know.

365
00:32:02,480 --> 00:32:03,560
But I do.

366
00:32:04,320 --> 00:32:06,120
I don't know what you're trying to do.

367
00:32:06,640 --> 00:32:09,240
But an ex-con like me,
I've turned my life around.

368
00:32:09,640 --> 00:32:10,640
Turned your life around?

369
00:32:11,440 --> 00:32:12,440
Yeah.

370
00:32:14,200 --> 00:32:15,320
And the unlicensed weed

371
00:32:15,400 --> 00:32:17,280
you're still selling
to kids in the village?

372
00:32:20,400 --> 00:32:22,200
Cops are all the same,
every single one of you.

373
00:32:22,960 --> 00:32:25,760
Honestly, the small-time weed selling
to village kids,

374
00:32:25,840 --> 00:32:27,000
I don't really care about.

375
00:32:27,080 --> 00:32:30,040
But if you don't tell me
what I want to know,

376
00:32:30,120 --> 00:32:31,960
I might start caring.

377
00:32:36,560 --> 00:32:37,880
What do you want to know?

378
00:32:40,280 --> 00:32:42,320
-look at this guys. Here.
-What?

379
00:32:42,600 --> 00:32:43,600
Here.

380
00:32:44,400 --> 00:32:46,920
-What?
-Good stuff, good stuff.

381
00:32:47,920 --> 00:32:49,560
My dad's gun.

382
00:32:50,320 --> 00:32:51,400
Wanna have some?

383
00:32:51,480 --> 00:32:53,120
-Wanna have some?
-Do you want to get it?

384
00:32:55,040 --> 00:32:56,160
do you want it?

385
00:32:56,240 --> 00:32:57,480
What the hell are you doing,
that's dangerous.

386
00:32:58,480 --> 00:33:00,000
Why does your dad even have a gun?

387
00:33:00,080 --> 00:33:01,400
Why not?

388
00:33:03,720 --> 00:33:05,280
Your dad's a total wimp.

389
00:33:05,720 --> 00:33:07,760
What? Is that true? Really?

390
00:33:10,240 --> 00:33:11,520
What the hell are you saying?

391
00:33:11,600 --> 00:33:13,040
My dad told me,

392
00:33:13,120 --> 00:33:14,480
back when he was studying with your dad,

393
00:33:14,920 --> 00:33:16,080
your dad got called a fag.

394
00:33:17,320 --> 00:33:20,000
-Really? Son of a fag!
-Son of a fag!

395
00:33:20,080 --> 00:33:22,520
-Alright cut it out.
-Son of a fag, you scum!

396
00:33:22,600 --> 00:33:24,160
What the hell, Chee!

397
00:33:24,240 --> 00:33:25,800
What's wrong with you?

398
00:33:25,880 --> 00:33:28,360
Chee, calm down!

399
00:33:29,120 --> 00:33:30,320
There's blood.

400
00:33:30,400 --> 00:33:32,200
So why did you take the fall for Chee?

401
00:33:38,920 --> 00:33:40,600
Can I actually say this?

402
00:33:40,680 --> 00:33:41,880
No one would believe me anyway.

403
00:33:41,960 --> 00:33:44,160
The only witnesses there were all drunk.

404
00:33:44,240 --> 00:33:45,760
Nobody actually saw what happened.

405
00:33:45,840 --> 00:33:46,880
You know how it is,

406
00:33:46,960 --> 00:33:48,240
in the end there always has to be

407
00:33:48,320 --> 00:33:49,520
a scapegoat to take the blame for Chee.

408
00:33:49,600 --> 00:33:51,200
That scapegoat was stupid enough

409
00:33:51,280 --> 00:33:52,480
to grab Chee's gun,
leaving his fingerprints.

410
00:33:52,560 --> 00:33:53,640
That scapegoat was me.

411
00:33:53,720 --> 00:33:55,200
You know what I had to go through?

412
00:33:55,280 --> 00:33:56,760
I had to drop out of university.

413
00:33:56,840 --> 00:33:58,200
And then four years in prison.

414
00:33:58,600 --> 00:33:59,840
Who's going to make that up to me?

415
00:33:59,920 --> 00:34:01,280
Can I go now?

416
00:34:17,720 --> 00:34:19,120
So busy, huh?

417
00:34:19,560 --> 00:34:21,240
Is the case closed yet?

418
00:34:53,840 --> 00:34:54,920
Hey,

419
00:34:55,240 --> 00:34:56,320
heard you got hit pretty bad.

420
00:34:56,400 --> 00:34:58,000
The bastard caught me off guard.

421
00:34:58,800 --> 00:35:00,440
Next time I see him
I'll take him down for good.

422
00:35:00,520 --> 00:35:01,880
Watch yourself. Stay careful.

423
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:04,080
I've got this.

424
00:35:07,160 --> 00:35:08,480
Oh hey, Jeans,

425
00:35:09,160 --> 00:35:10,640
you're one of Nai's customers too?

426
00:35:13,960 --> 00:35:15,200
I'll head off then.

427
00:35:16,120 --> 00:35:17,320
See you tonight.

428
00:35:18,320 --> 00:35:20,080
Fix up her lower part properly yeah.

429
00:35:34,480 --> 00:35:35,520
A mouth like that,

430
00:35:35,600 --> 00:35:36,760
he doesn't deserve a good death.

431
00:35:37,880 --> 00:35:38,920
Forget him.

432
00:35:39,280 --> 00:35:41,080
You heard about
the memorial party for Chee?

433
00:35:41,480 --> 00:35:43,040
Pretty much all the young people
in the village are going.

434
00:35:44,920 --> 00:35:46,160
And

435
00:35:46,720 --> 00:35:48,200
you're not scared
of a psycho killer being there?

436
00:35:50,120 --> 00:35:51,200
There'll be loads of people.

437
00:35:51,280 --> 00:35:52,480
What's there to be scared of?

438
00:35:53,240 --> 00:35:54,280
But what if

439
00:35:54,480 --> 00:35:55,800
the killer's at the party

440
00:35:57,160 --> 00:35:58,280
Then we mob them.

441
00:35:59,040 --> 00:36:01,160
Or maybe thank them.

442
00:36:04,640 --> 00:36:05,640
I'll go.

443
00:36:05,840 --> 00:36:07,120
A fun night like this,

444
00:36:07,960 --> 00:36:09,040
how could you miss it?

445
00:36:11,800 --> 00:36:12,920
I'll come pick you up then.

446
00:36:23,960 --> 00:36:25,200
I have a feeling
that Chee's case and Pan's

447
00:36:25,280 --> 00:36:26,680
disappearance are connected somehow.

448
00:36:30,240 --> 00:36:32,240
-Wait a moment.
-Sure, hurry up.

449
00:36:38,840 --> 00:36:39,880
Hey!

450
00:37:06,520 --> 00:37:07,680
Hello.

451
00:37:07,760 --> 00:37:08,920
I want to go to Chawin's house.

452
00:37:09,000 --> 00:37:10,400
I want to enter Chee's room.

453
00:37:10,800 --> 00:37:12,000
What can we do?

454
00:37:12,640 --> 00:37:13,680
Sure.

455
00:37:13,760 --> 00:37:14,880
I'll come get you.

456
00:38:03,920 --> 00:38:05,360
MEET ON THE ROCKS IN THE FOREST
IN THE AFTERNOON

457
00:38:05,440 --> 00:38:07,160
I HAVE SOMETHING IMPORTANT TO TALK ABOUT.
(OUR CHILD.)

458
00:38:07,240 --> 00:38:09,360
Jeans, I've found it.

459
00:38:11,360 --> 00:38:12,640
Then let's hurry and leave this place.

460
00:38:29,840 --> 00:38:30,840
Uncle.

461
00:38:33,480 --> 00:38:34,600
I missed you.

462
00:38:35,240 --> 00:38:36,440
Don't let anyone catch us,

463
00:38:36,520 --> 00:38:38,120
go wait in the room.

464
00:39:05,160 --> 00:39:06,560
See you at the party.

465
00:39:06,640 --> 00:39:07,680
Huh?

466
00:39:07,760 --> 00:39:08,880
We're not going together?

467
00:39:09,320 --> 00:39:10,400
Nai's coming to pick me up.

468
00:39:14,560 --> 00:39:15,800
When did you two get close?

469
00:39:16,720 --> 00:39:17,840
Recently,

470
00:39:17,920 --> 00:39:19,840
I went and got my motorcycle repaired.
Why?

471
00:39:22,480 --> 00:39:23,560
Nothing.

472
00:39:28,960 --> 00:39:29,960
It's nothing.

473
00:39:53,560 --> 00:39:55,720
Nai's here! Go all out boys!

474
00:39:57,080 --> 00:39:58,520
Woo!

475
00:39:59,040 --> 00:40:00,760
Come on, have some fun! Wooo!

476
00:40:01,000 --> 00:40:02,680
Woo!

477
00:40:05,560 --> 00:40:06,800
Go all out!

478
00:40:06,880 --> 00:40:08,880
The later it gets the wilder it gets!

479
00:40:09,400 --> 00:40:11,360
Woo!

480
00:40:11,880 --> 00:40:13,680
Cheers!

481
00:40:13,760 --> 00:40:16,040
Let's go! Woo!

482
00:40:24,560 --> 00:40:26,760
Let's go, guys! Come on, loosen up.

483
00:40:26,840 --> 00:40:27,840
Hey,

484
00:40:27,920 --> 00:40:29,520
what do you think about our handsome Nai?

485
00:40:29,600 --> 00:40:30,800
Did he get lucky with the slaughterhouse

486
00:40:30,880 --> 00:40:32,480
owner's granddaughter?

487
00:40:32,880 --> 00:40:34,000
Whoa,

488
00:40:34,080 --> 00:40:35,920
he's special.

489
00:40:37,120 --> 00:40:38,680
Hey! Hey!

490
00:40:38,760 --> 00:40:40,600
anyone want to try some good stuff?

491
00:40:41,280 --> 00:40:42,800
What good stuff?

492
00:40:42,880 --> 00:40:44,840
Can you show some respect
and honor the one who died?

493
00:40:44,920 --> 00:40:46,680
I am honoring him

494
00:40:47,120 --> 00:40:48,560
this is exactly what Chee liked!

495
00:40:49,320 --> 00:40:50,920
Anyone want to go have a chat with Chee?

496
00:40:51,840 --> 00:40:53,440
Woo!

497
00:40:54,800 --> 00:40:56,800
Come and get it.

498
00:40:58,160 --> 00:40:59,240
Hey, M.

499
00:40:59,320 --> 00:41:01,800
You think tonight a killer's gonna come
running after us

500
00:41:01,880 --> 00:41:03,040
like in a horror movie?

501
00:41:03,280 --> 00:41:04,560
Damn, that's scary as hell.

502
00:41:04,800 --> 00:41:06,240
If they show up just shoot their guts out.

503
00:41:09,240 --> 00:41:10,320
What?

504
00:41:10,760 --> 00:41:11,760
You came too?

505
00:41:11,840 --> 00:41:12,840
Come and meet Chee,

506
00:41:14,840 --> 00:41:15,840
what do you say?

507
00:41:17,920 --> 00:41:18,920
Want to give it a go?

508
00:41:19,880 --> 00:41:21,280
Try it.

509
00:41:32,680 --> 00:41:34,200
Here.

510
00:41:34,280 --> 00:41:35,280
Take it.

511
00:41:38,640 --> 00:41:39,880
One per each person.

512
00:41:39,960 --> 00:41:40,960
Here.

513
00:42:38,800 --> 00:42:40,840
Run!
